# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Viktor Zaverkin et al. (2024). Uncertainty-biased molecular dynamics for learning uniformly accurate interatomic potentials.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-024-01254-1  arXiv:2312.01416v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2312.01416v2 (sha256 3c9b4fc0e922611e...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 444 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zaverkin2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: Gaussian moment neural network (GM-NN) potentials
# obtained by active learning (up to 512 configurations; five repeats)
# with candidate pools from random selection, unbiased MD, metadynamics
# or uncertainty-biased MD (bias forces and bias stress), for alanine
# dipeptide (AMBER ff19SB labels) and MIL-53(Al) (CP2K PBE-D3(BJ)), and
# the test RMSEs of the final models of each experiment (Tables 1-2;
# means over five runs). CV-space coverage and auto-correlation times
# are exploration diagnostics.

