###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Evaluating uncertainty gradients increases inference time by a factor of 1.4-1.7 over unbiased MD (Discussion); total AL wall times are in the SI.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - All values are means over five AL repeats (standard deviations not encoded); stress RMSEs in MPa are converted exactly to GPa. The alanine-dipeptide reference is a classical force field (REF), not DFT.
# - Ensemble-based and distance-based uncertainty variants and the 1024-sample scaling runs are in the SI (Tables S1-S7). CV-space coverage and auto-correlation times are exploration diagnostics, not errors.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zaverkin2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

